Career Goal Reflection
I have an interest in how number can be manipulated and how the use of statistics can be used to solve real-world problems. I am particularly interested in learning how data can be analyzed and interpreted to help business make smarter more beneficial decisions. However, what I currently lack is real world experience and an understanding of what a true professional Data Scientist does and acts like on a daily basis. One of my primary goals in this stage of my academic learning is gaining experience working and collaborating alongside other Data Scientists on various projects and environments, while applying the technical skills I develop in college to problems that exist outside of the classroom. I also want to continue to improve my communication and networking skills. I acknowledge that to be a successful Data Scientist, I not only have to understand the technical skills, but have a set of transferable skills that allow me to work in a professional setting. I need to know how to communicate my findings with people who are not Data Scientists who do not have a technical background. I want to learn how to form connections with people already working in the industry and find mentorship within these people. I hope that I will continue to seek opportunities that allow me to become a more professional Data Scientist.Projects
